Christoph,

I do not have a lot of experience with Bioconductor but my experience  
is that for some chips (ie. mouse4302), the information is retrieved  
automatically but for the hugene10 chip it is not. My understanding  
is that it is because of the syntax of the file that is suggested by  
the CEL file (this is what I understood from the vignettes). If you  
want to set up for other people then the best way is probably to set  
up text files (or TinnR files) that have all the essential "start-up"  
commands on a "per chip" basis. This is pretty much the limit of my  
knowledge!

Sherri

